 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b1000001",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Correctivity — Single Movement Binary Classifier Training\n",
    "\n",
    "Trains a binary LSTM classifier on data produced by `CreateDataSetSingleMovement.ipynb`.\n",
    "\n",
    "| | |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Input shape | `(30 frames, 63 features)` — hand landmarks only |\n",
    "| Output | Single sigmoid unit — probability that the movement is occurring |\n",
    "| Loss | Binary cross-entropy |\n",
    "| Metrics | Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F1, ROC-AUC |\n",
    "| Export | `.h5` + TF.js conversion command |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why binary, not N-class?\n",
    "Each Correctivity model answers one question: *"Is this movement happening right now?"*  \n",
    "Binary framing gives cleaner precision/recall trade-off control via the confidence threshold,\n",
    "and avoids the need to enumerate all possible 'other' movements."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b1000002",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Imports"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b1000003",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import (\n",
    "    confusion_matrix, classification_report,\n",
    "    roc_curve, roc_auc_score, ConfusionMatrixDisplay\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "from tensorflow.keras.models import Sequential\n",
    "from tensorflow.keras.layers import LSTM, Dense, Dropout, BatchNormalization\n",
    "from tensorflow.keras.regularizers import l2\n",
    "from tensorflow.keras.callbacks import TensorBoard, EarlyStopping, ReduceLROnPlateau\n",
    "from tensorflow.keras.metrics import Precision, Recall"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b1000004",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Configuration\n",
    "\n",
    "Must match the values used in `CreateDataSetSingleMovement.ipynb`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b1000005",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "MOVEMENT_ID    = 'finger_extension_right'\n",
    "NO_SEQUENCES   = 50        # must match collection setting\n",
    "SEQUENCE_LENGTH = 30\n",
    "FEATURES        = 63       # 21 landmarks × 3 (x, y, z)\n",
    "\n",
    "DATA_PATH = os.path.join('..', 'datasets', 'correctivity', MOVEMENT_ID)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Training hyper-parameters\n",
    "EPOCHS       = 500\n",
    "BATCH_SIZE   = 32\n",
    "L2_NORM      = 0.001\n",
    "DROPOUT_RATE = 0.3\n",
    "TEST_SIZE    = 0.15\n",
    "\n",
    "# Confidence threshold used at inference time (tune after reviewing ROC curve)\n",
    "CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD = 0.7\n",
    "\n",
    "MODEL_SAVE_PATH = os.path.join('..', 'models', f'{MOVEMENT_ID}.h5')\n",
    "LOG_DIR = os.path.join('Logs', f'{MOVEMENT_ID}')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Movement : {MOVEMENT_ID}')\n",
    "print(f'Data path: {DATA_PATH}')\n",
    "print(f'Model out: {MODEL_SAVE_PATH}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b1000006",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Load Dataset"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b1000007",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sequences, labels = [], []\n",
    "\n",
    "for label, cls in enumerate(['target', 'other']):\n",
    "    cls_path = os.path.join(DATA_PATH, cls)\n",
    "    seq_dirs = sorted(os.listdir(cls_path), key=lambda x: int(x))\n",
    "    for seq_dir in seq_dirs:\n",
    "        window = []\n",
    "        for frame_num in range(SEQUENCE_LENGTH):\n",
    "            frame = np.load(os.path.join(cls_path, seq_dir, f'{frame_num}.npy'))\n",
    "            window.append(frame)\n",
    "        sequences.append(window)\n",
    "        labels.append(label)  # 1 = target, 0 = other  (see label order above)\n",
    "\n",
    "X = np.array(sequences, dtype=np.float32)   # (N, 30, 63)\n",
    "y = np.array(labels, dtype=np.float32)       # (N,)  binary\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'X shape : {X.shape}   (expected (N, {SEQUENCE_LENGTH}, {FEATURES}))')\n",
    "print(f'y shape : {y.shape}')\n",
    "print(f'Class balance — target: {y.sum():.0f}  other: {(1-y).sum():.0f}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b1000008",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Train / Test Split"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b1000009",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
    "    X, y, test_size=TEST_SIZE, stratify=y, random_state=42\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(f'Train: {X_train.shape[0]} samples   Test: {X_test.shape[0]} samples')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b1000010",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Build Model"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b1000011",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "model = Sequential([\n",
    "    LSTM(64, return_sequences=True, activation='tanh',\n",
    "         input_shape=(SEQUENCE_LENGTH, FEATURES), kernel_regularizer=l2(L2_NORM)),\n",
    "    LSTM(128, return_sequences=True, activation='tanh',\n",
    "         kernel_regularizer=l2(L2_NORM)),\n",
    "    Dropout(DROPOUT_RATE),\n",
    "    LSTM(64, return_sequences=False, activation='tanh',\n",
    "         kernel_regularizer=l2(L2_NORM)),\n",
    "    BatchNormalization(),\n",
    "    Dense(64, activation='relu', kernel_regularizer=l2(L2_NORM)),\n",
    "    Dense(32, activation='relu', kernel_regularizer=l2(L2_NORM)),\n",
    "    # Single sigmoid unit — outputs P(movement == target)\n",
    "    Dense(1, activation='sigmoid'),\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "model.compile(\n",
    "    optimizer='adam',\n",
    "    loss='binary_crossentropy',\n",
    "    metrics=[\n",
    "        'accuracy',\n",
    "        Precision(name='precision'),\n",
    "        Recall(name='recall'),\n",
    "    ]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "model.summary()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b1000012",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Train"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b1000013",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "os.makedirs(LOG_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "callbacks = [\n",
    "    TensorBoard(log_dir=LOG_DIR),\n",
    "    # Stop early if val_loss doesn't improve for 50 epochs\n",
    "    EarlyStopping(monitor='val_loss', patience=50, restore_best_weights=True, verbose=1),\n",
    "    # Halve LR when val_loss plateaus\n",
    "    ReduceLROnPlateau(monitor='val_loss', factor=0.5, patience=20, min_lr=1e-6, verbose=1),\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "history = model.fit(\n",
    "    X_train, y_train,\n",
    "    epochs=EPOCHS,\n",
    "    batch_size=BATCH_SIZE,\n",
    "    validation_split=0.15,\n",
    "    callbacks=callbacks,\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b1000014",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Training Curves"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b1000015",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(15, 4))\n",
    "\n",
    "for ax, metric, title in zip(\n",
    "    axes,\n",
    "    ['loss', 'accuracy', 'precision'],\n",
    "    ['Loss', 'Accuracy', 'Precision'],\n",
    "):\n",
    "    ax.plot(history.history[metric], label='train')\n",
    "    val_key = f'val_{metric}'\n",
    "    if val_key in history.history:\n",
    "        ax.plot(history.history[val_key], label='val')\n",
    "    ax.set_title(title)\n",
    "    ax.legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b1000016",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Save Model"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b1000017",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(MODEL_SAVE_PATH), exist_ok=True)\n",
    "model.save(MODEL_SAVE_PATH)\n",
    "print(f'Model saved to {MODEL_SAVE_PATH}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b1000018",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Evaluate on Test Set"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b1000019",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "y_prob = model.predict(X_test).flatten()           # sigmoid probabilities\n",
    "y_pred = (y_prob >= CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD).astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Confidence threshold : {CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD}')\n",
    "print()\n",
    "print(classification_report(y_test.astype(int), y_pred, target_names=['other', 'target']))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b1000020",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Confusion Matrix"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b1000021",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "cm = confusion_matrix(y_test.astype(int), y_pred)\n",
    "disp = ConfusionMatrixDisplay(confusion_matrix=cm, display_labels=['other', 'target'])\n",
    "disp.plot(cmap='Blues')\n",
    "plt.title(f'Confusion Matrix — threshold {CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD}')\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "tn, fp, fn, tp = cm.ravel()\n",
    "print(f'True Positives  (movement detected correctly) : {tp}')\n",
    "print(f'False Positives (false alarm)                 : {fp}')\n",
    "print(f'False Negatives (missed movement)             : {fn}')\n",
    "print(f'True Negatives  (rest correctly ignored)      : {tn}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b1000022",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## ROC Curve\n",
    "\n",
    "Use this to choose the `CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD` in `src/data/movements.ts`.  \n",
    "Higher threshold → fewer false positives (good for rep counting accuracy).  \n",
    "Lower threshold → fewer missed reps."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b1000023",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fpr, tpr, thresholds = roc_curve(y_test.astype(int), y_prob)\n",
    "auc = roc_auc_score(y_test.astype(int), y_prob)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(7, 5))\n",
    "plt.plot(fpr, tpr, label=f'AUC = {auc:.3f}')\n",
    "plt.plot([0, 1], [0, 1], 'k--', label='Random')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Mark the chosen threshold\n",
    "idx = np.argmin(np.abs(thresholds - CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD))\n",
    "plt.scatter(fpr[idx], tpr[idx], color='red', zorder=5,\n",
    "            label=f'Threshold = {CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD}')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.xlabel('False Positive Rate')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('True Positive Rate')\n",
    "plt.title(f'ROC Curve — {MOVEMENT_ID}')\n",
    "plt.legend()\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'AUC: {auc:.4f}  (target: > 0.95 before using model in production)')\n",
    "if auc < 0.95:\n",
    "    print('WARNING: AUC below 0.95 — collect more data or tune hyper-parameters before deploying.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b1000024",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Convert to TF.js\n",
    "\n",
    "Run the cell below to export the model for the React app.  \n",
    "Requires: `pip install tensorflowjs`\n",
    "\n",
    "The output is written to `correctivity-app/public/models/<MOVEMENT_ID>/`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b1000025",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "tfjs_output = os.path.join(\n",
    "    '..', 'correctivity-app', 'public', 'models', MOVEMENT_ID\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "convert_cmd = (\n",
    "    f'tensorflowjs_converter '\n",
    "    f'--input_format=keras '\n",
    "    f'\"{os.path.abspath(MODEL_SAVE_PATH)}\" '\n",
    "    f'\"{os.path.abspath(tfjs_output)}\"'\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Running:', convert_cmd)\n",
    "ret = os.system(convert_cmd)\n",
    "\n",
    "if ret == 0:\n",
    "    files = os.listdir(tfjs_output)\n",
    "    print(f'\\nTF.js model written to: {tfjs_output}')\n",
    "    print('Files:', files)\n",
    "    total_mb = sum(\n",
    "        os.path.getsize(os.path.join(tfjs_output, f))\n",
    "        for f in files\n",
    "    ) / 1e6\n",
    "    print(f'Total size: {total_mb:.2f} MB')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('Conversion failed. Make sure tensorflowjs is installed: pip install tensorflowjs')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b1000026",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Next Steps\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Check the ROC curve — adjust `CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD` if needed, then update `repStateMachineConfig.confidenceThreshold` in `correctivity-app/src/data/movements.ts`\n",
    "2. Confirm `public/models/<MOVEMENT_ID>/model.json` exists in the React app\n",
    "3. Start the React app (`npm run dev`) and verify the debug overlay shows confidence > 0.7 for the target movement\n",
    "4. Run the M0 exit-criteria test: 10 reps → confidence consistently > 0.7; still hand → confidence < 0.5"
   ]
  }
 ]
}
